MERGE (n:SynthesisAttribute {coordinate: 'L2-5'})
  SET n:MEFLens
  SET n += {
  `c_0_core_nature`: 'The fifth position completing tetralemma: not another lemma (which would still be within logic) but meaningful response integrating all four positions. After navigating is, is-not, both, neither - we emerge with not just answer but purposeful understanding. This is where logos becomes sophia - logic serves wisdom. The "why" reveals logical investigation isn\'t value-neutral - it serves purpose (truth-seeking, liberation, wisdom). TRANSCENDENT dimension of logic\'s realization - WHY ultimately framework matters. Second pole of [4↔5] oscillating culmination.',
  `c_0_essence`: 'Operates as fifth transcendent logical position where systematic investigation culminates in wisdom - synthesis revealing purpose enabled by contextual limits. Forms transcendent pole of [4↔5] oscillation in logic.',
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Operates as fifth transcendent logical position where systematic investigation culminates in wisdom - synthesis revealing purpose enabled by contextual limits. Forms transcendent pole of [4↔5] oscillation in logic.',
  `c_0_synthesis_nature`: 'Not mere answer but transformed understanding',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Wise consciousness; awareness integrating logical positions into purposeful understanding; the "why" of meaningful response',
  `c_1_description`: 'Synthesized response is where logical rigor culminates in wisdom. Following Nagarjuna, tetralemma isn\'t just formal logic but soteriological tool - it liberates from conceptual grasping. The response synthesizes: affirmation\'s content, negation\'s boundaries, paradox\'s creativity, transcendence\'s humility. This is "logical gnosis" - where systematic investigation generates transformative insight. Purpose revealed: logic serves life, understanding serves liberation. CRITICAL: Position 4 showed WHERE logic ends (contextual limits). Position 5 shows WHY logic matters (transcendent purpose). Together they complete logical realization.',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Organized as teleological completion: The synthesized response is WHY we engaged tetralemma - not for abstract logic but for purposeful knowing. Contains all four positions without being reducible to any - the wisdom integrating them. This is praxis - theory completed in practice, understanding manifested in wise action. The "why/purpose" as answer to ultimate teleological inquiry about logic itself.',
  `c_1_key_principles`: ['Logical Gnosis: Where logic becomes wisdom', 'Teleological Completion: Purpose of logical investigation revealed', 'Soteriological Logic: Nagarjuna\'s liberating methodology', 'Synthesized Understanding: Integrating all four lemmas', 'Meta-Logical Wisdom: Seeing framework as tool not truth', 'Praxis: Theory completed in wise action', 'Why-Answer: Ultimate purpose of systematic investigation'],
  `c_1_name`: 'Synthesized response (why)',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Crown (completion); synthesis symbol (⊕); lighthouse (guiding purpose); fruit (meaningful harvest); wise elder (integrated understanding)',
  `c_1_primary_designation`: 'Synthesized Response - Transcendent Logical Gnosis',
  `c_1_structure`: 'Organized as teleological completion: The synthesized response is WHY we engaged tetralemma - not for abstract logic but for purposeful knowing. Contains all four positions without being reducible to any - the wisdom integrating them. This is praxis - theory completed in practice, understanding manifested in wise action. The "why/purpose" as answer to ultimate teleological inquiry about logic itself.',
  `c_1_transformative_function`: 'Completes the cycle by offering actionable wisdom',
  `c_2_architectural_function`: 'Fifth position as gnosis/transcendence - cycle completes by recognizing logical framework\'s PURPOSE. Having exhausted logical space (all four corners) via Position 4\'s contextual limits, Position 5 achieves synthesis: not mechanical conclusion but wisdom-bearing understanding. This is meta-logical awareness - seeing tetralemma AS investigatory tool, not mistaking map for territory. Mirrors Level 0\'s archetypal five - TRANSCENDENT purpose. Forms transcendent pole of [4↔5] non-dual pair in logic.',
  `c_2_logical_bifurcation`: 'COMPLETING LOGIC\'S SPLIT: Position 4 gave contextual recognition (where/when framework applies). Position 5 gives transcendent realization (why ultimately it matters). Together they form complete logical wisdom: CONTEXTUAL (#4): The limits and applicability domain - recognizing framework\'s bounds. TRANSCENDENT (#5): The ultimate purpose - why investigation serves liberation. They OSCILLATE: Transcendent purpose requires contextual humility (knowing limits). Contextual limits receive meaning from transcendent purpose (why boundaries matter). Sophia (wisdom) requires both episteme (systematic knowing) bounded by recognition of its limits.',
  `c_2_notion_page_id`: '1d2a4797-123c-812b-8a9f-c1b9c746bf98',
  `c_2_omega_alpha_loop`: 'Position 5 returns to Position 0: Synthesized response (why logic matters) loops back to query (living question). WHY (5) asks WHAT QUESTIONS (0) now emerge? Omega and Alpha in logic - the synthesis generates new inquiry. Purpose (5) returns to potential (0) transformed.',
  `c_2_uuid`: 'c0b8bceb-ec69-57f4-bb75-a02f82c2c79c',
  `c_2_vertical_implication`: 'VERTICAL RESONANCE: Just as archetypal five creates transcendent dimension and transcendent final cause reveals ultimate purpose, transcendent synthesis reveals logic\'s meaning. Each level\'s Position 5 provides that level\'s ultimate realization.',
  `c_3_context_frame`: '0000',
  `c_3_dataset_branch`: 'parashakti-deep',
  `c_3_dataset_branch_label`: 'M2 Parashakti Deep',
  `c_3_practical_applications`: ['Wise Response: Integrating logical positions into meaningful answer', 'Purpose Recognition: Understanding why investigation matters', 'Liberation Practice: Using logic for freedom not bondage', 'Synthetic Thinking: Bringing all perspectives into unified understanding', 'Meta-Logical Reflection: Seeing frameworks as tools', 'Practical Wisdom: Completing analysis in appropriate action', 'Teleological Inquiry: Always asking "to what end?"'],
  `c_3_source_dataset`: 'bimba',
  `c_4_family`: 'L',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_ql_category`: 'implicate',
  `c_4_ql_operator_types`: ['structural'],
  `c_4_ql_position`: 5,
  `c_4_subsystem`: 2,
  `c_5_oscillatory_relationship`: '',
  `c_5_resonances`: ['Nagarjuna: Tetralemma as path to liberation', 'Sophia: Greek wisdom transcending mere knowledge', 'Prajna: Buddhist wisdom beyond conceptual understanding', 'Hegel: Absolute knowing as culmination', 'Aristotle: Phronesis (practical wisdom) vs. episteme', 'Plato: Dialectic culminating in Good beyond being', 'Archetypal Five: "Why" questions revealing ultimate purpose'],
  `c_5_systemic_resonance`: 'Jnana - integral knowing that emerges from logical completion',
  `coordinate_axis`: 'direct',
  `coordinate_parent`: 'L2',
  `l_0_base_index_6`: 2,
  `l_0_flat_index`: 17,
  `l_0_klein_square`: 'C',
